==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] and [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]

==Battleground==
*3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[King's Mimic]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**2 [[Zigge]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Zuche]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you've beaten [[Into the Future]] chapter 2, this stage should be simple.

All of the expected [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] are useful; [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]] for meatshielding, [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] for critting, and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] for general damage. [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] are helpful for the starting enemies, with [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho]] and [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Wall Cat]] also being good choices to bring for their respective [[Cat Combo|Combos]] with Catasaurus and Cameraman. Any legitimate [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] can be used effectively here as well.

